erasure.ask:
⚠️ **Delete my data**
We will delete everything the bot keeps about you:
• your prefix, favorites, integrations and Rich Presence app access;
• your recent tracks, Last.fm link and scrobble queue;
• your saved queue, favorite radios and personal radio list;
• your ID in the records of who changed a server's radios;
• your open panel sessions.

**What stays:**
• access and security records, for up to 6 months, to protect the service and comply with the law;
• if you are banned, the ban record, until the ban is lifted. Deleting your data does not lift the ban;
• while a player is running, the record of who requested each track and of the last Last.fm update, until the player stops;
• server settings and usage statistics, which are not tied to you;
• what was already sent to Last.fm, out of our reach. To end the bot's access to your account, revoke it at last.fm/settings/applications.

The hosting provider's backup copies may keep erased data for up to 4 weeks.
**This cannot be undone.** Do you really want to delete?
